TITLE:: NdefRackSpec
summary:: where the range of a control in the rack comes from, and how its value is written
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRack, Classes/NdefRackModule, Classes/ControlSpec, Classes/Spec

DESCRIPTION::
Every control in the rack needs a link::Classes/ControlSpec::, and the rack never
asks you for one. It looks, in this order:

numberedlist::
## the Ndef's own: JITLibExtensions' code::addSpec:: when that quark is
installed, which takes precedence the way it does there, then the code::spec::
given in the function, code::\freq.kr(110, spec: [20, 2000, \exp])::;
## the name in the global table, code::\freq.asSpec:: - but only when the
control's default fits inside it, so an lfo's code::\freq.kr(0.5):: is not given
a 20 Hz floor;
## a guess from the name and the default value.
::

code::
Ndef(\a, { SinOsc.ar(\freq.kr(330)) * \amp.kr(0.1) * \depth.kr(0.3) * \lfreq.kr(0.5) });

NdefRackSpec.origin(Ndef(\a), \freq);     // -> global
NdefRackSpec.origin(Ndef(\a), \depth);    // -> guess
NdefRackSpec.for(Ndef(\a), \depth);       // -> ControlSpec(0, 1)
NdefRackSpec.for(Ndef(\a), \lfreq);       // -> 0.01 to 100 Hz, exponential
::

The spec only sets where a bar can reach. A value set in code outside it stays
what it is: the bar sits at its end and the number says the truth.

subsection:: Units

The window writes a value in its units when the name says what they are -
link::#*unitFor::, link::#*readout:: - with no module saying anything:

table::
## strong::unit:: || strong::for::
## Hz, kHz || a frequency spec (20 to 20000 exponential, or units code::"Hz"::); the names freq, base, ref, formant, hpf, dark, rate and density; tone and bright when exponential
## bpm || bpm
## oct, with a sign || oct; shift reaching no further than 4
## s, ms || attack, decay, release, rise, fall, time, glen, sweep, snap, smooth, lag, predelay - unless the spec is a plain linear 0 to 1
## dB || floor, top; thresh when its range goes below 0 and no higher than 12
::

Anything else is a plain number: whole for a spec stepping by 1, two decimals
below 10, one above. On a bar whose name is its unit - oct, bpm - the
window leaves the unit off the number.

code::
NdefRackSpec.readout(\freq, \freq.asSpec, 1200);      // -> 1.2 kHz
NdefRackSpec.readout(\oct, nil, 0.25);                // -> +0.25 oct
NdefRackSpec.readout(\attack, nil, 0.01);             // -> 10 ms
NdefRackSpec.readout(\floor, [-120, -30].asSpec, -60); // -> -60.0 dB
::

subsection:: The guess

table::
## strong::the name has:: || strong::with a default of:: || strong::the range::
## code::wet1::, code::mix20:: - JITLib filter slots || anything || 0 to 1
## freq, cutoff, hz || 20 or more || 20 to 20000, exponential
## freq, cutoff, hz || above 0, below 20 || 0.01 to 100, exponential
## oct || within 4 || -4 to 4
## semi, transp || within 24 || -24 to 24
## db || up to 12 || -60 to 12
## time, attack, decay, release, dur, delay, lag, glide, slew, rise, fall || 0 to 10 || 0.001 to 10 s, exponential
## pan, bal, offset, bias || within 1 || -1 to 1
## step, len, count, num, chan, voices, bits || a whole number, 0 to 64 || 0 to twice that or 16, in steps of 1
::

With nothing in the name, the default decides: 0 is -1 to 1; 0 to 1 stays 0 to
1; -1 to 1 stays -1 to 1; above 1 is a twentieth to twenty times it,
exponentially.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: for
The spec for a control of a proxy.
ARGUMENT:: proxy
a link::Classes/NodeProxy::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the control's name.
ARGUMENT:: default
its default value; read from the proxy when nil.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/ControlSpec::.

METHOD:: origin
Which step the spec came from: code::\own::, code::\global:: or code::\guess::.

METHOD:: own
Step 1 alone: the Ndef's own spec for that name, or nil.

METHOD:: unitFor
The unit a control's value reads in, from its name and its spec - see link::#Units::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the control's name.
ARGUMENT:: spec
its link::Classes/ControlSpec::, or nil.
RETURNS:: code::"Hz"::, code::"oct"::, code::"s"::, code::"dB"::, or nil for a plain number.

METHOD:: readout
A value as the window writes it, with its unit: code::"1.2 kHz"::, code::"+0.25 oct"::, code::"10 ms"::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the control's name.
ARGUMENT:: spec
its link::Classes/ControlSpec::, or nil.
ARGUMENT:: value
the number; anything else is written as it is.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: guess
Step 3 alone, from a name and a default value.
code::
NdefRackSpec.guess(\attack, 0.01);
NdefRackSpec.guess(\whatever, 440);
::
